From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Store the white point, not the blue primary.

wayland_color_manager_primaries() accepts w_x and w_y, prints them in its
TRACE, and then stores b_x and b_y into primaries->w_x/w_y. The white point
of every output therefore equals its blue primary.

Consequences, in order:

  - WAYLAND_OUTPUT_PRIMARIES is set, so display.c reports srgb = FALSE and
    win32u/sysparams.c takes the "real chromaticity" branch when it builds the
    synthetic EDID, writing the bad white point into bytes 0x19..0x22.
  - DXVK reads that EDID back through libdisplay-info and publishes it as
    DXGI_OUTPUT_DESC1.WhitePoint; dxvk-nvapi publishes the same values as
    NV_HDR_CAPABILITIES.display_data.displayWhitePoint_x/y. The zero-coordinate
    D65 fallback in wsi_edid.h does not trigger, because the coordinates are
    non-zero, merely wrong.
  - An RGB->XYZ matrix derived from these primaries is singular: with the white
    point sitting on the blue primary, det() is exactly zero. Colours pushed
    through a chromatic adaptation built from it come out with the blue channel
    gained roughly fifty times relative to red and green.

Observed as Cyberpunk 2077 rendering its (yellow) epilepsy warning in violet
whenever HDR is enabled, from the first frame and on flat 2D content. Only HDR
is affected because the SDR path never consumes DESC1/NVAPI colorimetry.

Verified on this machine by decoding the synthetic EDID out of the game's
prefix registry: both attached outputs had W == B, (0.1436, 0.0557) and
(0.1465, 0.0645), where D65 is (0.3127, 0.3290).

Note that the TRACE prints the event arguments rather than the stored struct,
so the log looks entirely healthy while the wrong values are in memory. This is
why it survived so long.

Introduced by wine-hotfixes/wine-wayland/0242-winewayland-Remove-output_info-
structure.patch, which hand-expanded the COPY(w_x)/COPY(w_y) macro from patch
0096 and got the arguments wrong. Not an upstream Wine bug.

Authored by Claude (Anthropic AI) at the request of the repository owner.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
@@ -410,8 +410,8 @@
     primaries->g_y = round((g_y * 1e-6) * 1024);
     primaries->b_x = round((b_x * 1e-6) * 1024);
     primaries->b_y = round((b_y * 1e-6) * 1024);
-    primaries->w_x = round((b_x * 1e-6) * 1024);
-    primaries->w_y = round((b_y * 1e-6) * 1024);
+    primaries->w_x = round((w_x * 1e-6) * 1024);
+    primaries->w_y = round((w_y * 1e-6) * 1024);
 
     TRACE("primaries: {%lf, %lf, %lf, %lf, %lf, %lf, %lf, %lf}\n",
             r_x * 1e-6, r_y * 1e-6, g_x * 1e-6, g_y * 1e-6,
